// Command-permission publication: the one cross-package admission contract.
//
// Separate from `host` on purpose. A guest that never asks for this interface
// imports exactly the `host` instance it was built against, so adding the
// provider role did not renumber or retype any import an ordinary package
// already had: previously encoded packages keep instantiating.
interface command-permissions {
    /// Replace the deployment's command-permission grants.
    ///
    /// Only the package the deployment designates as its permission provider is
    /// handed a live instance; every other guest that imports this interface is
    /// answered `false`. Each entry is `"<identity> <node>"`, where `identity` is
    /// a dashed or compact lower-case UUID, or `*` for the default row that
    /// applies to a player the table has no explicit row for, and a node of `*`
    /// grants every node. The publication is all-or-nothing: an invalid or
    /// over-bound list is refused and the previous table stays in force.
    /// Synchronous, host-local, and refused during a pre-commit hook.
    publish: func(entries: list<string>) -> bool;
}
